Subject: JAGS fits centered funnel just fine
Message-ID: <6Yo3VDSXoQs.hgTxGpueAwAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/6Yo3VDSXoQs/m/hgTxGpueAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I ran the funnel in JAGS to follow along Daniel's section
in our course.

  model {
    for (n in 1:9) { x[n] ~ dnorm(0, 1 / exp(y / 2)^2) }
    y ~ dnorm(0, 1/3^2)
  }

and it appears to fit well out of the box (this is using R2jags):

> jags(data=list(), inits=list(list(), list(), list(), list()),
       model.file="funnel.jags", parameters.to.save=c("x", "y"),
       n.chains=4, DIC=FALSE)

