By "hard constraint", I took you to mean that

  lognormal(y | mu, tau) -> 0 as y -> 0

whereas the uniform doesn't have that property.  Is
there more to it than that, or was the "no" about my
saying that y = 0.0025 was close to zero?  It's not
nearly as close as you can get on a computer in double
precision --- that's 1e-300 or so.

