Literally just histograms of both samples plotted on top of each other.
As seen in Figure 3 of http://arxiv.org/pdf/1312.0906.pdf (hard numbers
in Table I) the Metropolis-within-Gibbs did better than Random Walk
but still had some trouble getting down into the neck (and was much
slower than HMC).  I’m guessing that you’d see a lighter tail in the
Gibbs samples, but perhaps not much.

